Sure, I'd be happy to help you generate multiple arrays using the `forEach()` method in JavaScript. Here's an example that demonstrates how to create multiple arrays based on a given array of objects:

```javascript
// Sample array of objects
const data = [
  { id: 1, name: 'John', age: 30 },
  { id: 2, name: 'Jane', age: 25 },
  { id: 3, name: 'Bob', age: 20 },
  { id: 4, name: 'Alice', age: 35 },
];

// Function to generate arrays based on a property
function generateArrays(data, property) {
 const arrays = {};

 data.forEach((item) => {
    if (!arrays[item[property]]) {
      arrays[item[property]] = [];
    }
    arrays[item[property]].push(item);
  });

  return arrays;
}

// Generate arrays based on the 'age' property
const arraysByAge = generateArrays(data, 'age');

// Output the generated arrays
console.log(arraysByAge);

/*
Output:
{
  30: [{ id: 1, name: 'John', age: 30 }],
  25: [{ id: 2, name: 'Jane', age: 25 }],
  20: [{ id: 3, name: 'Bob', age: 20 }],
  35: [{ id: 4, name: 'Alice', age: 35 }]
}
*/
```

In this example, the `generateArrays()` function takes an array of objects and a property name as arguments. It then uses the `forEach()` method to iterate over each object in the array and generates arrays based on the specified property. The resulting object contains arrays grouped by the unique values of the given property.

You can modify the `generateArrays()` function to return an array of arrays instead of an object if needed. Here's an example:

```javascript
function generateArrays(data, property) {
 const arrays = [];
 const uniqueValues = new Set();

 data.forEach((item) => {
    if (!uniqueValues.has(item[property])) {
      uniqueValues.add(item[property]);
      arrays.push([]);
    }
    arrays[arrays.length - 1].push(item);
  });

  return arrays;
}

// Generate arrays based on the 'age' property
const arraysByAge = generateArrays(data, 'age');

// Output the generated arrays
console.log(arraysByAge);

/*
Output:
[
  [{ id: 1, name: 'John', age: 30 }],
  [{ id: 2, name: 'Jane', age: 25 }],
  [{ id: 3, name: 'Bob', age: 20 }],
  [{ id: 4, name: 'Alice', age: 35 }]
]
*/
```

