Yes, I am aware of the npm package `nodemailer-outlook`. This package is a transport plugin for Nodemailer, a popular module for sending emails in Node.js. The `nodemailer-outlook` package allows you to use Outlook as the email service provider for sending emails through Nodemailer.

To use this package, you will first need to install it using npm:
```
npm install nodemailer-outlook
```
Once the package is installed, you can use it in your Node.js code as follows:
```
const nodemailer = require('nodemailer');
const outlook = require('nodemailer-outlook');

// create a Nodemailer transporter using the Outlook transport plugin
const transporter = nodemailer.createTransport(outlook({
  auth: {
    user: 'your-email@outlook.com',
    pass: 'your-password'
  }
}));

// define the email message
const message = {
  from: 'your-email@outlook.com',
  to: 'recipient@example.com',
  subject: 'Hello from Outlook',
  text: 'This is a test email sent using Nodemailer and Outlook.'
};

// send the email
transporter.sendMail(message, (error, info) => {
  if (error) {
    console.log('Error sending email:', error);
  } else {
    console.log('Email sent:', info.response);
  }
});
```
This code creates a Nodemailer transporter using the `nodemailer-outlook` transport plugin, and then sends an email using the transporter. The `auth` object in the `createTransport` method is used to authenticate with the Outlook email service using your email address and password.

